WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Turn a face upside down and a strange change may almost disappear.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Turn it upright and suddenly you see what was always there.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Psychologists call this the Thatcher illusion. Later studies show the story is more complicated than one special face-processing trick.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
It tells us perception depends on context. But the illusion does not prove a meditation recording fixes attention.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Before buying a routine, try one free twelve-minute session. Keep the observation.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Compare the promise with the evidence. Then decide.
